# Root-agnostic kernel guarantees
#
# This builder ships a kernel that contains NO root solution: the
# kernelsu-gki.config fragment (the only place CONFIG_KSU=y is set) is excluded
# by default, and the flashable zip replaces the kernel blob only, leaving the
# ramdisk untouched. Rooting is entirely the user's decision, taken after the
# kernel is installed.
#
# For that decision to stay open, the kernel must keep the facilities every
# external root solution relies on. All of these are =y in the stock ACK
# gki_defconfig; they used to be re-stated by the (now excluded) kernelsu
# fragment, so pin them here instead. build-kernel.sh skips symbols already
# effective, so this fragment is idempotent -- its job is to make the guarantee
# explicit and to give the workflow's verification step something to assert.
#
#   MODULES / MODULE_UNLOAD  loading an out-of-tree root LKM (e.g. KernelSU in
#                            LKM mode) and unloading it again
#   KPROBES                  syscall hooking used by KernelSU-style solutions
#   KALLSYMS / KALLSYMS_ALL  symbol lookup those hooks need at runtime
#   EXT4_FS                  ext4_unregister_sysfs and friends
#
# Nothing here enables root by itself; it only preserves the ability to add one.

CONFIG_MODULES=y
CONFIG_MODULE_UNLOAD=y
CONFIG_KPROBES=y
CONFIG_KALLSYMS=y
CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL=y
CONFIG_EXT4_FS=y
